    "author": "Paul Morris",
    "description": "Reproduction study — inspired by Clairnote SN (Paul Morris, 2018). Major-third 2-line staff at E/G#; the internal floating ledgers for D/F#/A# plus the C ledger are override templates (per the operator reference). The C ledger shows for C/C#/D; the operator's rule also lists A#/B, but those sit below the C-boundary where the platform's C-aligned ledger regions would place the ledger at the wrong (lower) C across an intervening staff line, so they are trimmed and the limitation is documented as a gap. Uniform duration-carrying ovals. Clairnote's alternative key signatures (E2) are exercised via the platform's notehead-chords signature (set 010, itself inspired by Clairnote DN's stacked signatures) — this follows Clairnote's stacked-signature layout design but is NOT identical to Clairnote's specific accidental-sign signatures. Clairnote's alternative CLEF form is not shown in the sources, so no clef is authored (omission); its alternative accidental signs need the unimplemented accidental enhancement (E4) — documented deviation. Design CC BY-SA 4.0; no code ported from clairnote.ly. Built from the public gallery description/image; not endorsed by or derived from the original.",
    "systemName": "Clairnote SN",
    "systemCreator": "Paul Morris",
    "systemYear": 2018,
    "sourceUrl": "https://musicnotation.org/system/clairnote-sn-paul-morris/",
    "reproductionStudy": true,
